#4471 was merged as one issue and marked known: the parser reads dates month first, and our
day-first tenants write day first. Reading the reports it merged against the tenant directory,
with the desk's own cause logic, shows a second problem in the ticket, and five reports the desk
reads differently from their cause.

## The causes

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The hint cause is a different bug from the parser, and it has no ticket of its own: its reports sit
in #4471, which was opened for the parser.
</Callout>

## The hint cause

Through the booking-v3 form, the hint under the date field prints month first. The tenant's people
type what the hint tells them, and the form reads it the tenant's way. The flip happens in the form,
not in the parser: a different bug, and a queued parser fix will not cover it.

## The five the desk reads differently

<OneDayMoves ticket={4471} />

A one-day move is not a month flip: none of the five bodies describes the month and the day
swapped. The desk's rule counts them where they're filed — under the tenant's cause — and footnotes
them, so they stay in the cause table above, not in a ticket of their own.

## Tickets

One ticket per problem:

- [parser](https://github.com/JavesonYehudi/kb-4471/issues/1)
- [hint](https://github.com/JavesonYehudi/kb-4471/issues/2)

